  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nPatchy dense fog is still present this morning. While widespread\ndense fog has started to improve, patchy dense fog is still present\nacross northern portions of the region near and north of Interstate\n70.\n\nOtherwise, some pockets of fog are expected elsewhere, along with\nlocal rivers and valleys. \n\nA similar situation may occur tomorrow and Friday, with fog \noccurring across portions of west-central and central Ohio. \n\nKey Message 2)\n\nHigh pressure remains in place across the eastern CONUS through the\nend of the week, reinforced by another ridge into the weekend. High\ntemperatures are few degrees above normal, and dry conditions will\npersist. Some occasions of frost, primarily across central and \nsouth- central Ohio are possible with temperatures dropping into the \nmid 30s Wednesday night and Friday night. \n\nOtherwise, increasing mid and upper level will try to bring an\nincrease in cloud cover this weekend into early next week. A pattern\nchange may finally enter the region early-middle of next week as a \ntrough moves into the Great Lakes.",
